diff --git a/HEGEL_REPORT.md b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ca3fc7d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/HEGEL_REPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,151 @@
+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report
+
+Property-based tests were added with [hegel](https://hegel.dev) (`hegeltest`
+dev-dependency). The previous quickcheck suite (`tests/quickcheck.rs`) was
+ported to hegel and the `quickcheck` dev-dependency removed. Note: `hegeltest`
+requires rustc 1.86, above the crate's declared `rust-version = "1.65.0"`; it
+was added with `cargo add --dev --ignore-rust-version` (dev-dependency only —
+whether that MSRV bump for tests is acceptable is a maintainer decision).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+In `tests/test_round_trip.rs`:
+
+1. **`pbt_roundtrip_generated_document`** — any generated `Yaml` document
+   (nested arrays/hashes/scalars; strings drawn from arbitrary Unicode text,
+   number/bool/null lookalikes, radix-prefixed strings, YAML indicator
+   characters, Unicode separators `U+0085`/`U+2028`/`U+2029`/`U+FEFF`; hash
+   keys include complex `?` keys) survives emit → load unchanged.
+2. **`pbt_roundtrip_generated_document_multiline`** — the same roundtrip with
+   `multiline_strings(true)` (literal block scalar emission).
+3. **`pbt_string_scalar_type_and_content_preserved`** — a `Yaml::String`
+   scalar always reloads as a `String` with identical content, however much it
+   looks like a number, boolean, null, date, or YAML syntax.
+4. **`pbt_number_scalar_roundtrip`** — `Yaml::Integer` (full `i64` range) and
+   `Yaml::Real` (loader-canonical float strings, `.inf`/`.nan` forms)
+   roundtrip unchanged.
+5. **`pbt_multi_document_stream_roundtrip`** — a stream of several documents,
+   each emitted with its own `---` header, loads back as the same sequence.
+6. **`pbt_array_of_weird_strings_roundtrip`** — port of the quickcheck
+   property `test_check_weird_keys`: an array of arbitrary strings
+   roundtrips (same 100-case count as the quickcheck default).
+
+In `tests/basic.rs`:
+
+7. **`pbt_load_arbitrary_text_never_panics`** — `YamlLoader::load_from_str`
+   returns `Ok`/`Err` but never panics, on arbitrary Unicode text and on
+   YAML-syntax token soup.
+8. **`pbt_emitted_documents_reparse_to_same_value`** — any document the
+   loader accepts (from arbitrary/YAML-ish text) can be re-emitted, and the
+   emitted YAML parses back to the same value (load → emit → load identity).
+9. **`pbt_alias_resolves_to_anchored_value`** — an alias `*a` resolves to
+   exactly the value of its anchor `&a`.
+10. **`pbt_decoder_never_panics_on_arbitrary_bytes`** — `YamlDecoder` never
+    panics (or hangs) on arbitrary byte input under all three standard
+    decoding traps.
+
+Every property that overlaps a known bug excludes exactly the pinned buggy
+input class, with comments referencing the canonical `known_bug_*` test.
+
+## Test results
+
+- All 10 properties above pass at the default 100 cases and in an exploratory
+  10x run (1000 cases per property).
+- Liveness was verified by temporarily inverting a property:
+  hegel reported and shrank the counterexample to the minimal `Integer(0)`.
+- The full pre-existing suite (unit tests, scanner, emitter, spec tests,
+  yaml-test-suite (402 cases), doc-tests) passes. The `tests/yaml-test-suite`
+  git submodule was not initialized in this checkout and had to be fetched
+  (`git submodule update --init`) for that harness to run at all.
+- **7 pinned known-failure tests fail deliberately and deterministically**
+  (every generated case hits the bug): six `known_bug_*` tests in
+  `tests/test_round_trip.rs` fail on every run, and one hang reproducer in
+  `tests/basic.rs` is `#[ignore]`d (running it hangs forever, which would
+  take the whole suite down). These document the bugs below and must stay
+  failing until the bugs are fixed.
+
+## Suspected bugs
+
+All found by the properties above, none fixed (per instructions); each is
+pinned by a deterministic test:
+
+1. **`0o…` octal-looking strings change type**
+   (`known_bug_octal_like_string_changes_type`): `need_quotes`
+   (src/emitter.rs) quotes `0x`-prefixed strings but not `0o`-prefixed ones,
+   while `Yaml::from_str` parses `0o…` as octal. `String("0o7")` is emitted
+   bare and reloads as `Integer(7)`.
+2. **`+.inf` strings change type**
+   (`known_bug_plus_dot_inf_string_changes_type`): `parse_f64` accepts
+   `+.inf`/`+.Inf`/`+.INF` but `need_quotes` does not quote them.
+   `String("+.inf")` reloads as `Real("+.inf")`.
+3. **Integer-looking `Real` values change type**
+   (`known_bug_integer_looking_real_changes_type`): `Yaml::Real` is emitted
+   verbatim with no check that the text still reads back as a float.
+   `!!float 5` loads as `Real("5")`, which is emitted as bare `5` and reloads
+   as `Integer(5)`.
+4. **Multiline mode: leading-space lines break block scalars**
+   (`known_bug_multiline_leading_space_line`): a literal-block line starting
+   with a space breaks indentation detection. `" a\nb"` produces output that
+   fails to parse ("wrongly indented line in block scalar"); `"\n a"`
+   silently reloads as `"\na"`.
+5. **Multiline mode: trailing newlines lost**
+   (`known_bug_multiline_trailing_newlines_lost`): literal blocks are always
+   emitted with clip chomping (`|`/`|-`, never `|+`), so `"a\n\n\n"` reloads
+   as `"a\n\n"` and `"\n\n"` reloads as `"\n"`.
+6. **Multiline mode: multiline string as mapping key corrupts the document**
+   (`known_bug_multiline_string_as_hash_key`): a scalar key containing `\n`
+   is emitted as a block scalar in key position; `{"a\nb": ~}` emits as
+   `|-\n  a\n  b: ~`, which reloads as the single string `"a\nb: ~"`.
+7. **`YamlDecoder` hangs forever on short expanding input**
+   (`known_bug_decoder_hangs_on_short_expanding_input`, `#[ignore]`d):
+   `decode_loop` (src/yaml.rs) reserves `input.len()` output bytes and grows
+   the output by `input.len() / 10` bytes on `OutputFull`. `String::reserve`
+   only guarantees capacity ≥ len + additional, so when `input.len() / 10` is
+   smaller than the next character's UTF-8 width, the loop makes no progress:
+   inputs shorter than 40 bytes whose UTF-8 output outgrows the reservation
+   hang forever. Minimal reproducer: `FF FE 34 12 34 12 34 12` (UTF-16LE
+   `ሴሴሴ`, 8 bytes in, 9 UTF-8 bytes out). Found by property 10, whose live
+   version now draws `binary().min_size(40)` to stay clear of the hang.
+
+## Unsound properties abandoned
+
+- **Roundtrip of arbitrary `Yaml::Real(String)` values** — unsound as
+  originally conceived: `Real` is emitted verbatim, so only strings the
+  loader itself would classify as `Real` can possibly roundtrip
+  (`Real("hello")` is not a reachable loader value). The generator was
+  constrained to loader-canonical float strings (`format!("{f:?}")` of finite
+  floats plus `.inf`/`.nan` forms). Within that domain the property is sound
+  — and still caught bug 3 via the `!!float 5` loader path.
+- **Roundtrip of documents containing `Yaml::BadValue` or `Yaml::Alias`** —
+  unsound: the emitter has no representation for them (`BadValue` emits `~`,
+  i.e. null; `Alias` emits nothing). Generators never produce them, and the
+  load → emit → load property skips loader-produced `BadValue` documents
+  (empty documents, invalid tagged scalars, unresolved aliases).
+- **`load_from_str` ≡ `load_from_iter` equivalence** — not written:
+  tautological, one delegates to the other.
+
+## Skill feedback
+
+- The workflow paid off in order: reading the emitter's `need_quotes` before
+  writing generators (per "generate at the encode-set boundary") is directly
+  what surfaced the `0o`/`+.inf` holes, and the "cursed strings" angles from
+  the property catalogue (number/bool/null lookalikes, Unicode separators)
+  were the right target list.
+- The Rust reference was accurate throughout: `hegeltest` vs `hegel` naming,
+  `--ignore-rust-version` for the MSRV clash, the recursive-generator
+  `compose!`+`BoxedGenerator` pattern (recursive `#[hegel::composite]` indeed
+  does not compile), and `one_of!` accepting heterogeneous generator types
+  all worked exactly as documented.
+- The guidance on pinning real bugs (boosted generator so every case fails →
+  deterministic red) and on excluding pinned classes from siblings with
+  cross-referencing comments kept the suite in a useful state: 10 live green
+  properties, 7 precise red/ignored pins.
+- The "special case: process-aborting failures" advice generalized well to a
+  *hang* (decoder bug): `#[ignore]` + documented reproducer was the right
+  move since libtest has no per-test timeout. The skill could mention hangs
+  explicitly alongside stack-overflow/OOM aborts, and that a hang inside a
+  property can masquerade as "hegel being slow" — a `timeout`-wrapped run of
+  the single test distinguishes the two quickly.
+- Minor friction: there is no global case-count override, so the 10x
+  exploratory run required a temporary `sed` over the attributes, as the
+  reference itself suggests.
diff --git a/tests/basic.rs b/tests/basic.rs
index d980bea..6187e1c 100644
--- a/tests/basic.rs
+++ b/tests/basic.rs
@@ -525,3 +525,163 @@ fn test_nominal_float_parse() {
         assert!(it.as_str().is_some());
     }
 }
+
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Property-based tests (hegel)
+// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+use hegel::generators::{self, BoxedGenerator, Generator};
+
+/// Arbitrary text biased towards YAML syntax: either fully arbitrary Unicode
+/// text or a concatenation of YAML-significant fragments, so the scanner and
+/// parser see plenty of structurally interesting input.
+fn yamlish_text() -> BoxedGenerator<'static, String> {
+    const TOKENS: &[&str] = &[
+        "- ", "-", ": ", ":", "? ", "&a ", "*a", "!!int ", "!!str ", "!!float ", "!!bool ",
+        "!t ", "|", "|-", "|+", ">", ">-", "#c", "\n", "\n  ", "\n\t", " ", "'", "\"", "[",
+        "]", "{", "}", ",", "---", "...", "%YAML 1.2", "%TAG ! !e", "\t", "a", "b", "0", "1.5",
+        "null", "~", "true", "\\", "\"\\n\"", "''", "\u{feff}", "\r\n", "&", "*", "!", "@",
+        "`", "0o7", "+.inf", "e", ".",
+    ];
+    hegel::one_of!(
+        generators::text(),
+        generators::vecs(generators::sampled_from(
+            TOKENS.iter().map(|s| (*s).to_string()).collect::<Vec<_>>()
+        ))
+        .max_size(30)
+        .map(|v| v.concat()),
+    )
+    .boxed()
+}
+
+/// The loader must return `Ok` or `Err`, but never panic, whatever the input.
+#[hegel::test]
+fn pbt_load_arbitrary_text_never_panics(tc: hegel::TestCase) {
+    let s = tc.draw(yamlish_text());
+    drop(YamlLoader::load_from_str(&s));
+}
+
+/// Whether a loaded value is hit by a known emitter bug. Each class is
+/// pinned by a canonical failing `known_bug_*` test in
+/// `tests/test_round_trip.rs`; see there for details.
+fn hits_known_emitter_bug(doc: &Yaml) -> bool {
+    match doc {
+        // `known_bug_octal_like_string_changes_type` and
+        // `known_bug_plus_dot_inf_string_changes_type`.
+        Yaml::String(s) => {
+            s.strip_prefix("0o")
+                .map_or(false, |rest| i64::from_str_radix(rest, 8).is_ok())
+                || matches!(s.as_str(), "+.inf" | "+.Inf" | "+.INF")
+        }
+        // `!!float 5` loads as `Real("5")`, which is re-emitted as an
+        // integer: `known_bug_integer_looking_real_changes_type`.
+        Yaml::Real(s) => s.parse::<i64>().is_ok(),
+        Yaml::Array(v) => v.iter().any(hits_known_emitter_bug),
+        Yaml::Hash(h) => h
+            .iter()
+            .any(|(k, v)| hits_known_emitter_bug(k) || hits_known_emitter_bug(v)),
+        _ => false,
+    }
+}
+
+/// Whether a loaded value contains `BadValue` (empty documents, invalid
+/// tagged scalars, unresolved aliases). `BadValue` is not representable by
+/// the emitter (it is emitted as `~`), so roundtrip properties skip it.
+fn contains_badvalue(doc: &Yaml) -> bool {
+    match doc {
+        Yaml::BadValue => true,
+        Yaml::Array(v) => v.iter().any(contains_badvalue),
+        Yaml::Hash(h) => h
+            .iter()
+            .any(|(k, v)| contains_badvalue(k) || contains_badvalue(v)),
+        _ => false,
+    }
+}
+
+/// Any document the loader accepts must be re-emittable as valid YAML that
+/// parses back to the same value (load → emit → load is the identity on
+/// loaded values).
+#[hegel::test]
+fn pbt_emitted_documents_reparse_to_same_value(tc: hegel::TestCase) {
+    let s = tc.draw(yamlish_text());
+    let Ok(docs) = YamlLoader::load_from_str(&s) else {
+        tc.reject();
+    };
+    for doc in &docs {
+        if contains_badvalue(doc) || hits_known_emitter_bug(doc) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        let mut emitted = String::new();
+        YamlEmitter::new(&mut emitted).dump(doc).unwrap();
+        let reparsed = YamlLoader::load_from_str(&emitted).unwrap_or_else(|e| {
+            panic!("emitted YAML failed to reparse: {e}\ninput: {s:?}\nemitted: {emitted:?}")
+        });
+        assert_eq!(reparsed.len(), 1, "emitted: {emitted:?}");
+        assert_eq!(&reparsed[0], doc, "emitted: {emitted:?}");
+    }
+}
+
+/// An alias (`*a`) resolves to the same value as its anchor (`&a`).
+#[hegel::test]
+fn pbt_alias_resolves_to_anchored_value(tc: hegel::TestCase) {
+    let items: Vec<i64> = tc.draw(generators::vecs(generators::integers::<i64>()).max_size(5));
+    let body = items
+        .iter()
+        .map(ToString::to_string)
+        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
+        .join(", ");
+    let src = format!("- &a [{body}]\n- *a");
+    let docs = YamlLoader::load_from_str(&src).unwrap();
+    assert_eq!(docs.len(), 1);
+    let expected = Yaml::Array(items.into_iter().map(Yaml::Integer).collect());
+    assert_eq!(docs[0][0], expected);
+    assert_eq!(docs[0][1], expected);
+}
+
+/// The byte-stream decoder must never panic (or hang) on arbitrary bytes,
+/// whichever decoding trap is configured.
+#[cfg(feature = "encoding")]
+#[hegel::test]
+fn pbt_decoder_never_panics_on_arbitrary_bytes(tc: hegel::TestCase) {
+    use yaml_rust2::yaml::{YAMLDecodingTrap, YamlDecoder};
+    // KNOWN BUG exclusion: `decode_loop` (src/yaml.rs) grows the output by
+    // `input.len() / 10` bytes on `OutputFull`, and `String::reserve` only
+    // guarantees capacity >= len + additional. When `input.len() / 10` is
+    // smaller than the next character's UTF-8 width (up to 4 bytes), no
+    // progress is made and decoding spins forever, so inputs shorter than 40
+    // bytes can hang. `.min_size(40)` avoids the hang; the bug is pinned by
+    // the ignored `known_bug_decoder_hangs_on_short_expanding_input` test
+    // below.
+    let bytes: Vec<u8> = tc.draw(generators::binary().min_size(40));
+    let trap = match tc.draw(generators::integers::<u8>().max_value(2)) {
+        0 => YAMLDecodingTrap::Ignore,
+        1 => YAMLDecodingTrap::Strict,
+        _ => YAMLDecodingTrap::Replace,
+    };
+    drop(YamlDecoder::read(bytes.as_slice()).encoding_trap(trap).decode());
+}
+
+/// KNOWN FAILURE (hang): `decode_loop` (src/yaml.rs) reserves `input.len()`
+/// output bytes up front and, whenever the output is full, grows it by
+/// `input.len() / 10` bytes. `String::reserve` only guarantees capacity >=
+/// len + additional, so whenever `input.len() / 10` is smaller than the next
+/// character's UTF-8 width the loop makes no progress and decoding hangs
+/// (inputs shorter than 40 bytes are affected; for inputs shorter than 10
+/// bytes the growth is exactly zero). Minimal reproducer: UTF-16LE BOM +
+/// `ሴሴሴ` (8 bytes in, 9 bytes of UTF-8 out).
+///
+/// This test is `#[ignore]`d rather than left failing because it never
+/// terminates and would hang the whole test suite. Run it manually with
+/// `cargo test -- --ignored known_bug_decoder` to observe the hang.
+#[cfg(feature = "encoding")]
+#[test]
+#[ignore = "hangs forever: decode_loop makes no progress on short expanding input"]
+fn known_bug_decoder_hangs_on_short_expanding_input() {
+    use yaml_rust2::yaml::{YAMLDecodingTrap, YamlDecoder};
+    let bytes: &[u8] = &[0xFF, 0xFE, 0x34, 0x12, 0x34, 0x12, 0x34, 0x12];
+    drop(
+        YamlDecoder::read(bytes)
+            .encoding_trap(YAMLDecodingTrap::Replace)
+            .decode(),
+    );
+}
